1
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:11,400
Who am I? You sure you want to know?

2
00:03:11,608 --> 00:03:14,862
The story of my life
is not for the faint of heart.

3
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:17,656
If somebody said
it was a happy little tale...

4
00:03:17,865 --> 00:03:22,327
... if somebody told you I was just an
average ordinary guy, not a care in the world...

5
00:03:22,494 --> 00:03:24,288
... somebody lied.

6
00:03:25,163 --> 00:03:28,750
But let me assure you, this
like any story worth telling...

7
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:30,335
... is all about a girl.

8
00:03:31,211 --> 00:03:35,674
That girl. The girl next door.
Mary Jane Watson.

9
00:03:35,841 --> 00:03:38,927
The woman I've loved
since before I even liked girls.

10
00:03:39,094 --> 00:03:41,763
I'd like to tell you that's me
next to her.

11
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:43,932
Aw, heck, I'd even take him.

12
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:47,853
Hey! Stop the bus!

13
00:03:48,854 --> 00:03:50,022
That's me.

14
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:52,107
Tell him to stop! Please!

15
00:03:52,316 --> 00:03:53,525
Stop!

16
00:03:53,734 --> 00:03:55,944
Hey! Stop the bus!

17
00:03:56,111 --> 00:03:59,198
Stop the bus! He's been chasing us
since Woodhaven Blvd.

18
00:03:59,364 --> 00:04:00,616
Catch a cab, Parker!

19
00:04:05,078 --> 00:04:07,873
Thank you. I'm sorry I'm late.

20
00:04:13,295 --> 00:04:14,588
What a geek!

21
00:04:15,255 --> 00:04:19,468
- Don't even think about it.
- You're so lame, Parker.

22
00:04:19,635 --> 00:04:21,220
Would you date him?

23
00:04:39,112 --> 00:04:41,323
Midtown High seniors.

24
00:04:41,490 --> 00:04:45,202
No wandering. Proceed direct...
Knock it off.

25
00:04:45,494 --> 00:04:48,956
Remember, it is a privilege
to be here.

26
00:04:49,331 --> 00:04:52,584
We're guests of Columbia University's
Science Department.

27
00:04:52,793 --> 00:04:55,003
So behave accordingly.

28
00:04:55,170 --> 00:04:58,215
Let's not have a repeat
of our trip to the planetarium.

29
00:04:58,423 --> 00:05:00,050
Come on, stay together.

30
00:05:00,217 --> 00:05:03,136
Proceed up the steps
and into the building.

31
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:07,349
- Where were you?
- Checking out the library.

32
00:05:07,516 --> 00:05:10,060
- Looking at the books.
- Yeah, right.

33
00:05:11,812 --> 00:05:15,649
- Dad would you ask Hoskins to drive around the corner please.
- Why?

34
00:05:15,858 --> 00:05:17,651
The entrance is right there.

35
00:05:17,818 --> 00:05:21,530
Dad these are public school kids,
I'm not showing up for the field trip in a Rolls.

36
00:05:21,738 --> 00:05:24,074
You want me to trade in my care for a Jetta

37
00:05:24,241 --> 00:05:27,035
just because you flunked out of every private school I ever sent you to?

38
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:30,372
- It wasn't for me.
- Of course it was.

39
00:05:31,039 --> 00:05:35,377
- Don't ever be ashamed of who you are.
- I'm not ashamed of who I am.

40
00:05:35,586 --> 00:05:36,879
It's just...

41
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:38,505
Just what, Harry?

42
00:05:38,714 --> 00:05:40,215
Forget it.

43
00:05:43,218 --> 00:05:44,553
Pete!

44
00:05:44,970 --> 00:05:47,049
- Hi, Harry.
- Hey, man. What's up?

45
00:05:47,328 --> 00:05:50,559
- Harry! Won't you be needing this?
- Thanks Dad.

46
00:05:51,518 --> 00:05:55,480
- Um, Peter may I introduce my father, Norman Osborn.
- I've heard so much about you.

47
00:05:55,689 --> 00:05:59,151
- It's a great honour to meet you sir.
- Harry tells me you're quite the science whiz.

48
00:05:59,401 --> 00:06:02,237
Y'know, I'm something of a scientist myself.

49
00:06:02,404 --> 00:06:05,574
I read all your research on nanotechnology.
Really Brilliant.

50
00:06:05,741 --> 00:06:08,785
- You understood it?
- Yes, I wrote a paper on it.

51
00:06:08,994 --> 00:06:12,289
Impressive.
Your parents must be very proud.

52
00:06:12,456 --> 00:06:17,002
- I live with my aunt and uncle, they are proud.
- Hey, you two! Let's move!

53
00:06:17,169 --> 00:06:20,839
- Nice to meet you.
- Hope to see you again.

54
00:06:23,175 --> 00:06:26,678
- He doesn't seem so bad.
- Not if you're a genius.

55
00:06:26,845 --> 00:06:28,805
I think he wants to adopt you.

56
00:06:28,972 --> 00:06:33,710
There are over 32,000 known species
of spider in the world.

57
00:06:33,894 --> 00:06:37,689
They're in the order Araneae,
divided into three suborders.

58
00:06:37,898 --> 00:06:38,982
That's amazing!

59
00:06:39,149 --> 00:06:43,070
This is the most advanced electron
microscope in the eastern seaboard.

60
00:06:43,403 --> 00:06:45,447
It's unreal.

61
00:06:45,614 --> 00:06:48,408
Arachnids from all three
groups possess...

62
00:06:48,617 --> 00:06:52,120
...varying strengths which help them
in their constant search for food.

63
00:06:52,329 --> 00:06:56,542
For example, the Delena spider,
family Sparassidae...

64
00:06:56,708 --> 00:07:00,879
...has the ability to jump
to catch its prey.

65
00:07:01,046 --> 00:07:02,798
For the school paper?

66
00:07:07,302 --> 00:07:12,307
Next, we have the net web spider,
family Filistatidae...

67
00:07:12,516 --> 00:07:14,393
...genus Kukulcania.

68
00:07:14,643 --> 00:07:18,981
It spins an intricate funnel shaped web whose strands
have a tensile strength

69
00:07:19,189 --> 00:07:24,444
...proportionately equal to the type of high tension wire...

70
00:07:24,903 --> 00:07:26,572
- Leave him alone.
- Or what?

71
00:07:26,738 --> 00:07:29,741
Or his father will fire your father.

72
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:32,494
What's Daddy gonna do? Sue me?

73
00:07:32,661 --> 00:07:35,164
What is going on?

74
00:07:35,330 --> 00:07:38,417
The next person who talks
will fail this course. I kid you not.

75
00:07:38,625 --> 00:07:40,627
- This grass spider...
- Let's go.

76
00:07:40,794 --> 00:07:44,965
...hunts using reflexes with
nerve-conduction velocity so fast...

77
00:07:45,174 --> 00:07:48,677
...that some researchers believe
it almost borders on precognition.

78
00:07:48,844 --> 00:07:51,013
-Those guys are jerks.
-...an imminent awareness of danger...

79
00:07:51,221 --> 00:07:52,973
A spider-sense.

80
00:07:53,599 --> 00:07:55,267
Hey, look at that spider.

81
00:07:55,434 --> 00:07:59,855
Some spiders change colors
to blend into their environment.

82
00:08:00,105 --> 00:08:02,024
It's a defense mechanism.

83
00:08:02,191 --> 00:08:05,485
Peter, what makes you think
I'd want to know that?

84
00:08:05,652 --> 00:08:06,862
Who wouldn't?

85
00:08:07,029 --> 00:08:10,866
Over five painstaking years,
Columbia's genetic research facility has...

86
00:08:11,033 --> 00:08:15,412
- You gonna talk to her now?
- Oh, no. Come on. You talk to her.

87
00:08:15,621 --> 00:08:20,375
With these DNA blueprints, we have
begun what was once thought impossible.

88
00:08:20,584 --> 00:08:24,254
- Disgusting.
- Yeah, hateful little things.

89
00:08:24,463 --> 00:08:25,839
I love them!

90
00:08:26,381 --> 00:08:28,050
Yeah, me too.

91
00:08:29,009 --> 00:08:32,888
You know, spiders can change
their color...

92
00:08:33,055 --> 00:08:36,892
...to blend into their environment.
- Really?

93
00:08:37,059 --> 00:08:41,188
- Yeah, it's a defense mechanism.
- Cool.

94
00:08:41,396 --> 00:08:44,775
...transfer RNA
to encode an entirely new genome...

95
00:08:44,942 --> 00:08:48,070
...combining the genetic
information from all three...

96
00:08:48,237 --> 00:08:52,908
...into these 15 genetically
designed super-spiders.

97
00:08:53,075 --> 00:08:54,576
There's 14.

98
00:08:55,035 --> 00:08:56,411
I beg your pardon?

99
00:08:56,578 --> 00:08:59,122
- One's missing.
- Yeah.

100
00:09:02,042 --> 00:09:04,670
I guess the researchers
are working on that one.

101
00:09:05,170 --> 00:09:09,883
Do you know that this is the largest
electron microscope on the eastern seaboard?

102
00:09:10,050 --> 00:09:14,137
You were talking throughout
that woman's entire presentation.

103
00:09:14,304 --> 00:09:16,056
Let's talk about how we listen.

104
00:09:20,143 --> 00:09:23,612
I don't know what it's like
at those fancy private schools...

105
00:09:24,439 --> 00:09:26,316
...but at Midtown High...

106
00:09:32,948 --> 00:09:38,537
Hey, Could I take your picture?
I need one with a student in it.

107
00:09:38,704 --> 00:09:40,164
- Sure, yeah.
- Great.

108
00:09:40,372 --> 00:09:42,666
Where do you want me?
Over here?

109
00:09:42,875 --> 00:09:44,209
Yeah, that's great.

110
00:09:44,626 --> 00:09:46,295
Don't make me look ugly.

111
00:09:46,670 --> 00:09:48,505
That's impossible.

112
00:09:55,762 --> 00:09:57,014
Perfect.

113
00:10:04,771 --> 00:10:06,315
- Is that good?
- Great.

114
00:10:11,862 --> 00:10:13,238
That's great.

115
00:10:18,827 --> 00:10:20,829
M.J., let's go!

116
00:10:22,372 --> 00:10:24,958
Wait. Thanks!

117
00:10:38,430 --> 00:10:41,183
Parker, let's do it.

118
00:10:57,908 --> 00:11:01,370
We've solved the horizon glide
and the multi-G balance issues.

119
00:11:01,537 --> 00:11:04,081
I've already seen the glider.

120
00:11:04,498 --> 00:11:06,542
That's not what I'm here for.

121
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:09,419
General Slocum, good to see you again.

122
00:11:10,254 --> 00:11:12,422
Mr. Balkan, Mr. Fargas.

123
00:11:12,673 --> 00:11:14,508
- Norman.
- Mr. Osborn.

124
00:11:14,675 --> 00:11:18,220
Always a pleasure to have
our board of directors pay us a little visit.

125
00:11:18,428 --> 00:11:21,849
I want to see the progress report on
Human performance enhancers.

126
00:11:21,903 --> 00:11:25,024
We tried vapour inhalation with rodent subjects.

127
00:11:25,025 --> 00:11:26,904
They showed an 800 percent increase in strength.

128
00:11:26,939 --> 00:11:28,564
- Excellent.
- Any side effects?

129
00:11:28,730 --> 00:11:29,815
-In one trial yes.
-It was an aberration.

130
00:11:29,982 --> 00:11:32,651
All the tests since
have been successful.

131
00:11:32,818 --> 00:11:36,572
In the trial that went wrong, what happen?
what were the side effects?

132
00:11:36,738 --> 00:11:39,074
Violence, aggression...

133
00:11:39,741 --> 00:11:40,993
...and insanity.

134
00:11:41,159 --> 00:11:43,912
- What do you recommend?
- That was only one test.

135
00:11:44,163 --> 00:11:48,000
With the exception of Dr. Strom our entire staff
certifies the product

136
00:11:48,167 --> 00:11:51,086
...ready for human testing.
- Dr. Stromm?

137
00:11:52,421 --> 00:11:56,091
We need to take the whole line
back to formula.

138
00:11:57,342 --> 00:11:59,761
- Back to formula?
- Dr. Osborn.

139
00:12:00,929 --> 00:12:02,764
I'm going to be frank with you.

140
00:12:03,015 --> 00:12:07,853
I never supported your program. We
have my predecessor to thank for that.

141
00:12:08,020 --> 00:12:10,772
Norman, the General gave the go-ahead
to request aerospace

142
00:12:10,939 --> 00:12:13,859
...to build a prototype
of their exoskeleton design.

143
00:12:14,193 --> 00:12:18,113
- They test in two weeks.
- And if your so-called performance enhancers

144
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:22,367
...have not had a successful
human trial by that date...

145
00:12:22,618 --> 00:12:26,997
...I'm gonna pull your funding.
I'm going to give it to them.

146
00:12:28,790 --> 00:12:30,459
Gentlemen. Ladies.

147
00:12:35,547 --> 00:12:40,969
And the Lord said, "Let there be light."
And voil�! There is light.

148
00:12:41,220 --> 00:12:43,305
Forty soft, glowing watts of it.

149
00:12:43,472 --> 00:12:48,310
Good boy. God will be thrilled.
Just don't fall on your ass.

150
00:12:48,644 --> 00:12:51,063
I'm already on my ass, May.

151
00:12:51,230 --> 00:12:55,734
When the plant's senior electrician
is laid off after 35 years...

152
00:12:55,901 --> 00:12:58,612
...what would you call it?
I am on my ass.

153
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:01,156
Hand me that dish. The green one.

154
00:13:01,406 --> 00:13:04,159
The corporation is downsizing
the people...

155
00:13:04,618 --> 00:13:06,495
...and upsizing their profits.

156
00:13:06,745 --> 00:13:09,665
Oh, Ben, you'll get another job
somewhere.

157
00:13:10,666 --> 00:13:13,585
Well, let's look
in the paper and see.

158
00:13:14,711 --> 00:13:17,506
There are the want ads.
What do we got here?

159
00:13:17,673 --> 00:13:19,299
Computer...

160
00:13:19,508 --> 00:13:23,262
Computer salesman, computer engineer,
computer analyst.

161
00:13:23,428 --> 00:13:27,182
My Lord, even the computers
need analysts these days.

162
00:13:27,474 --> 00:13:32,771
I'm 68. I'm too old for computers, and
besides, I have a family to provide for.

163
00:13:32,980 --> 00:13:35,858
I love you. And Peter loves you.

164
00:13:36,108 --> 00:13:39,361
You're the most responsible man
I've ever known.

165
00:13:39,611 --> 00:13:44,032
We've been down-and-out before.
But somehow, we survive.

166
00:13:45,158 --> 00:13:49,454
Hi, sweetie. You're just...
Just in time for dinner.

167
00:13:49,663 --> 00:13:52,207
How you doing? How was the field trip?

168
00:13:52,374 --> 00:13:55,210
I don't feel well.
I'm gonna go to sleep.

169
00:13:55,377 --> 00:13:57,880
- You won't have a bite?
- No thanks, had a bite.

170
00:13:58,046 --> 00:14:00,465
Did you get some pictures, Peter?

171
00:14:01,300 --> 00:14:04,136
I gotta crash. Everything's fine.

172
00:14:05,554 --> 00:14:07,139
What's that all about?

173
00:14:28,410 --> 00:14:30,621
In this recombination lab...

174
00:14:30,787 --> 00:14:35,417
...we use synthesized transfer RNA
to encode an entirely new genome...

175
00:14:35,626 --> 00:14:38,670
...combining the genetic
information from all three...

176
00:14:38,879 --> 00:14:43,675
... into these 15 genetically
designed super-spiders.

177
00:14:58,148 --> 00:15:02,110
Dr. Osborn, please.
The performance enhancers aren't ready.

178
00:15:02,277 --> 00:15:05,614
The data just doesn't justify
this test.

179
00:15:05,781 --> 00:15:09,451
Now, I'm asking you for the last time.
We can't do this.

180
00:15:09,618 --> 00:15:11,829
Don't be a coward.

181
00:15:12,287 --> 00:15:14,873
Risks are part of laboratory science.

182
00:15:15,082 --> 00:15:18,794
Let me reschedule,
with the proper medical staff and a volunteer.

183
00:15:19,002 --> 00:15:21,463
- If you just give me two weeks...
- Two weeks?

184
00:15:21,630 --> 00:15:26,134
In two weeks? We'll have lost the contract
to Quest and OSCORP will be dead.

185
00:15:26,301 --> 00:15:29,054
Sometimes you gotta
do things yourself.

186
00:15:29,221 --> 00:15:31,890
- Get me the Promachloraperazine.
- For what?

187
00:15:32,057 --> 00:15:35,811
It begins catalyzation when the vapor
hits the bloodstream.

188
00:15:38,730 --> 00:15:40,399
40,000 years of evolution...

189
00:15:40,566 --> 00:15:44,319
...and we've barely tapped
the vastness of human potential.

190
00:15:58,167 --> 00:15:59,501
Oh, that's cold.

191
00:16:57,976 --> 00:16:59,228
Norman?

192
00:17:03,732 --> 00:17:05,025
Norman!

193
00:17:15,744 --> 00:17:17,079
Oh, my God.

194
00:17:18,580 --> 00:17:19,998
Oh, my God!

195
00:17:22,668 --> 00:17:24,503
Oh, my God! Norman!

196
00:17:40,894 --> 00:17:42,521
Back to formula?

197
00:18:17,139 --> 00:18:18,640
Weird.

198
00:18:29,568 --> 00:18:30,944
- Peter?
- Yeah?

199
00:18:31,153 --> 00:18:32,905
Are you all right?

200
00:18:34,823 --> 00:18:36,450
I'm fine.

201
00:18:37,034 --> 00:18:40,412
- Any better this morning? Any change?
- Change?

202
00:18:41,413 --> 00:18:43,332
Yep. Big change.

203
00:18:43,499 --> 00:18:47,503
- Well, hurry up. You're going to be late.
- Right.

204
00:19:05,896 --> 00:19:07,272
Okay.

205
00:19:11,985 --> 00:19:15,781
- Goodness me!
- Jeez. I thought you were sick.

206
00:19:16,323 --> 00:19:17,658
- I got better.
- See?

207
00:19:17,824 --> 00:19:18,172
- Bye, guys.

208
00:19:18,483 --> 00:19:21,542
- You haven't eaten anything, have you got your lunch money?
- Yeah I've got it.

209
00:19:21,704 --> 00:19:25,040
Hey Michaelangelo don't forget
we're painting the kitchen right after school. Got it?

210
00:19:25,207 --> 00:19:28,001
Sure, Uncle Ben.
Don't start without me.

211
00:19:28,210 --> 00:19:30,295
And don't start up with me.

212
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:35,551
Teenagers. Raging hormones.
They never change.

213
00:19:36,510 --> 00:19:40,222
You're trash!
You're always going to be trash just like her.

214
00:19:40,389 --> 00:19:43,976
- I have to go to school.
- Who's stopping you?

215
00:20:01,368 --> 00:20:03,036
Hi, M.J.

216
00:20:03,912 --> 00:20:05,414
Hey, M.J.

217
00:20:05,664 --> 00:20:10,210
I don't know if you realize this, but
we've been neighbors since I was 6.

218
00:20:10,377 --> 00:20:13,714
And I was wondering
if we could get together sometime?

219
00:20:13,922 --> 00:20:15,215
I got the car. Hop in.

220
00:20:15,382 --> 00:20:18,260
Do something fun?
Or, I don't know.

221
00:20:18,468 --> 00:20:22,306
I thought it'd be time
to get to know each other.

222
00:20:22,556 --> 00:20:23,807
Or not.

223
00:20:29,271 --> 00:20:31,982
Sorry, Parker, the bus is full!

224
00:20:33,525 --> 00:20:36,069
- Stop the bus!
- Catch a cab!

225
00:20:36,486 --> 00:20:38,113
Tell him to stop.

226
00:20:38,780 --> 00:20:40,782
- Check him out!
- Dork!

227
00:21:03,263 --> 00:21:04,515
Dad!

228
00:21:04,973 --> 00:21:06,850
Dad, are you all right?

229
00:21:07,684 --> 00:21:08,977
Harry.

230
00:21:12,314 --> 00:21:14,316
What are you doing on the floor?

231
00:21:14,483 --> 00:21:15,817
I don't know.

232
00:21:16,652 --> 00:21:18,987
Have you been there all night?

233
00:21:20,989 --> 00:21:22,241
Last night I was...

234
00:21:24,576 --> 00:21:25,828
What?

235
00:21:27,079 --> 00:21:28,848
- I don't remember.
- Mr. Osborn?

236
00:21:29,180 --> 00:21:31,375
Sir, I asked her to wait in the foyer.

237
00:21:31,542 --> 00:21:35,879
- My father's not feeling well...
- Mr. Osborn, Dr. Stromm is dead.

238
00:21:36,046 --> 00:21:37,089
What?

239
00:21:37,256 --> 00:21:40,843
They found his body this morning
in the lab. He's been murdered, sir.

240
00:21:41,009 --> 00:21:44,388
- What are you talking about?
- And the flight suit and the glider...

241
00:21:44,555 --> 00:21:46,557
- What about it?
- It's been stolen, sir.

242
00:22:11,498 --> 00:22:14,251
Wow! Great reflexes!

243
00:22:15,127 --> 00:22:17,296
- Thanks.
- No problem.

244
00:22:18,380 --> 00:22:22,301
Hey, you have blue eyes.
I didn't notice without your glasses.

245
00:22:23,051 --> 00:22:24,720
You just get contacts?

246
00:22:31,476 --> 00:22:33,645
Well, see you.

247
00:23:15,437 --> 00:23:18,941
- What happened?
- He's freaking weird.

248
00:23:19,399 --> 00:23:20,776
Did you see that?

249
00:23:22,361 --> 00:23:24,029
Parker?

250
00:23:55,894 --> 00:23:58,313
- It's a fight!
- Think you're pretty funny don't you, freak?

251
00:23:58,480 --> 00:24:01,483
- Flash it was just an accident.
-My fist breaking your teeth is the accident.

252
00:24:01,692 --> 00:24:04,403
-C'mon Flash, stop.
-I don't want to fight you Flash.

253
00:24:04,570 --> 00:24:07,990
- I wouldn't want to fight me neither.
- Kick his ass.

254
00:24:26,884 --> 00:24:28,218
Help him, Harry.

255
00:24:33,182 --> 00:24:34,683
How'd he do that?

256
00:24:35,767 --> 00:24:37,019
Which one?

257
00:24:37,186 --> 00:24:38,562
He's all yours, man.

258
00:24:54,077 --> 00:24:55,787
Flash, get up!

259
00:24:57,414 --> 00:25:00,542
Jesus, Parker, you are a freak.

260
00:25:02,461 --> 00:25:03,962
That was amazing.

261
00:25:04,880 --> 00:25:06,882
I'm out of here. Come on.

262
00:26:52,070 --> 00:26:53,113
Go, web!

263
00:26:54,698 --> 00:26:56,325
Fly.

264
00:26:57,910 --> 00:26:59,995
Up, up and away, web.

265
00:27:01,580 --> 00:27:02,998
Shazam!

266
00:27:03,582 --> 00:27:04,833
Go! Go!

267
00:27:05,083 --> 00:27:06,835
Go, web, go!

268
00:27:39,952 --> 00:27:41,703
Tallyho.

269
00:28:25,622 --> 00:28:28,208
- Is she back with the beer yet?
- What?

270
00:28:28,417 --> 00:28:29,668
Bring me some beer.

271
00:28:29,877 --> 00:28:32,421
- Get up off your ass.
- I paid for beer...

272
00:28:32,588 --> 00:28:34,089
- Stop yelling.
- Stop it!

273
00:28:34,256 --> 00:28:36,592
You're as stupid as your mother.

274
00:28:38,510 --> 00:28:41,054
Where's she going?
Where you going?

275
00:28:42,139 --> 00:28:45,475
The dishes aren't done.
Somebody's gotta do dishes.

276
00:28:45,684 --> 00:28:48,979
- Why don't you do them?
- Get in here and do the dishes.

277
00:28:49,188 --> 00:28:53,317
- You do them. They're yours, anyway.
- I'm going out!

278
00:28:53,525 --> 00:28:56,028
- Were you listening to that?
- No.

279
00:28:56,361 --> 00:28:59,615
Well, I heard, but I was
just taking out the trash.

280
00:28:59,781 --> 00:29:02,534
I guess you can always hear us.

281
00:29:02,701 --> 00:29:04,995
Everybody shouts.

282
00:29:05,454 --> 00:29:07,581
Your aunt and uncle don't.

283
00:29:07,748 --> 00:29:10,292
Oh, they can scream
pretty good sometimes.

284
00:29:11,710 --> 00:29:15,923
Listen, M.J., about today
at school with Flash...

285
00:29:16,173 --> 00:29:17,799
You really freaked us out.

286
00:29:18,008 --> 00:29:20,260
I'm sorry. Is he okay?

287
00:29:20,552 --> 00:29:24,515
He's just happy you didn't give him
a black eye for graduation.

288
00:29:27,601 --> 00:29:30,812
So where are you going
after you graduate?

289
00:29:35,567 --> 00:29:37,861
I wanna move into the city.

290
00:29:38,779 --> 00:29:43,575
And hopefully, get a job
as a photographer.

291
00:29:43,742 --> 00:29:46,578
Work my way through college.

292
00:29:47,579 --> 00:29:48,914
What about you?

293
00:29:49,081 --> 00:29:51,083
Headed for the city too.

294
00:29:51,792 --> 00:29:54,044
Can't wait to get out of here.

295
00:29:55,212 --> 00:29:56,713
I wanna...

296
00:29:57,965 --> 00:29:59,466
What?

297
00:30:02,302 --> 00:30:04,555
No, come on. Try me.

298
00:30:05,472 --> 00:30:06,974
I wanna...

299
00:30:08,100 --> 00:30:09,434
...act...

300
00:30:10,602 --> 00:30:12,104
...on-stage.

301
00:30:12,688 --> 00:30:14,523
Really?

302
00:30:14,898 --> 00:30:17,067
Oh, that's perfect.

303
00:30:17,359 --> 00:30:19,903
You were awesome
in all the school plays.

304
00:30:20,237 --> 00:30:22,072
- Really?
- Yeah.

305
00:30:22,698 --> 00:30:25,701
I cried like a baby
when you played Cinderella.

306
00:30:26,201 --> 00:30:28,412
Peter, that was first grade.

307
00:30:28,912 --> 00:30:30,414
Well...

308
00:30:30,956 --> 00:30:32,457
...even so.

309
00:30:33,458 --> 00:30:35,377
Sometimes...

310
00:30:36,211 --> 00:30:37,880
...you know people.

311
00:30:39,047 --> 00:30:42,634
You can just see what's coming.

312
00:30:45,721 --> 00:30:48,473
What do you see coming for you?

313
00:30:51,059 --> 00:30:52,728
I don't know.

314
00:30:55,063 --> 00:30:59,735
Whatever it is, it's something
I never felt before.

315
00:31:03,322 --> 00:31:06,241
And what for me?

316
00:31:06,408 --> 00:31:07,743
For you?

317
00:31:09,161 --> 00:31:11,914
You're gonna light up Broadway.

318
00:31:13,415 --> 00:31:14,750
You know...

319
00:31:19,129 --> 00:31:21,757
...you're taller than you look.

320
00:31:21,924 --> 00:31:23,467
I hunch.

321
00:31:25,719 --> 00:31:27,221
Don't.

322
00:31:30,766 --> 00:31:34,311
Hey, M.J.! Come take a ride
in my new birthday present.

323
00:31:35,395 --> 00:31:36,688
Come on.

324
00:31:37,773 --> 00:31:39,107
I gotta go.

325
00:31:39,942 --> 00:31:41,109
Bye.

326
00:31:41,777 --> 00:31:44,446
- Oh, my God, it's gorgeous!
- Yeah, right.

327
00:31:44,613 --> 00:31:46,615
- Look at it!
- Hop in.

328
00:31:46,782 --> 00:31:49,034
Oh, my God. What a cool car!

329
00:31:49,284 --> 00:31:50,869
Pretty tight, huh?

330
00:31:51,286 --> 00:31:55,624
Wait till you hear the sound system.
Hey, don't scratch the leather.

331
00:31:57,376 --> 00:31:58,627
Cool car.

332
00:33:31,345 --> 00:33:33,388
What's going on in there?

333
00:33:33,597 --> 00:33:36,225
I'm exercising.
I'm not dressed, Aunt May.

334
00:33:36,391 --> 00:33:40,062
Well, you're acting
so strangely, Peter.

335
00:33:40,354 --> 00:33:42,439
Okay. Thanks.

336
00:34:13,262 --> 00:34:16,598
Something's bothering him.
Maybe he's too embarrased to tell me what it is.

337
00:34:16,765 --> 00:34:19,434
Maybe I'm too embarrassed to ask him.

338
00:34:20,227 --> 00:34:22,271
I don't know, I just don't know anymore.

339
00:34:22,688 --> 00:34:25,232
I'm going to the downtown library,
I'll see you later.

340
00:34:25,440 --> 00:34:28,819
- Wait. I'll drive you there, buddy.
- I'll take the train.

341
00:34:28,986 --> 00:34:32,239
No, I need the exercise.
Go on. Go, go, go.

342
00:34:43,292 --> 00:34:46,753
- Thanks for the ride, Uncle Ben.
- Now wait a minute, we need to talk.

343
00:34:46,920 --> 00:34:51,300
- We can talk later.
- Well, we can talk now. If you let me.

344
00:34:52,176 --> 00:34:54,428
What do we have to talk about?
Why now?

345
00:34:54,595 --> 00:34:58,640
Because we haven't talked at all for so long,
your Aunt May and I don't even know who you are any more.

346
00:34:58,807 --> 00:35:03,812
You shirk your chores. You have all
those weird experiments in your room.

347
00:35:03,979 --> 00:35:08,108
- You start fights at school.
- I didn't start that fight, I told you that.

348
00:35:08,317 --> 00:35:11,278
- Well you sure as hell finished it.
- What was I supposed to do, run away?

349
00:35:11,487 --> 00:35:14,490
No, you're not supposed
to run away, but...

350
00:35:14,656 --> 00:35:19,203
But, Pete look, you're changing. I know,
I went through exactly the same thing at your age.

351
00:35:19,411 --> 00:35:21,413
No. Not exactly.

352
00:35:21,768 --> 00:35:25,501
Peter... these are the years
when a man changes...

353
00:35:25,667 --> 00:35:29,671
...into the man he's gonna become
the rest of his life.

354
00:35:29,838 --> 00:35:32,925
Just be careful who you change into.

355
00:35:34,468 --> 00:35:38,972
This guy, Flash Thompson,
he probably deserved what happened.

356
00:35:39,515 --> 00:35:42,226
But just because you can
beat him up...

357
00:35:42,684 --> 00:35:44,937
...doesn't give you the right to.

358
00:35:45,604 --> 00:35:50,859
Remember, with great power
comes great responsibility.

359
00:35:51,443 --> 00:35:56,448
Are you afraid that I'm going to turn into some
kind of criminal? Quit worrying about me, okay?

360
00:35:56,615 --> 00:36:00,035
Something's different.
I'll figure it out. Stop lecturing, please.

361
00:36:00,327 --> 00:36:04,540
I don't mean to lecture and I don't mean to
preach. And I know I'm not your father--

362
00:36:04,706 --> 00:36:07,543
Then stop pretending to be!

363
00:36:11,630 --> 00:36:12,881
Right.

364
00:36:15,843 --> 00:36:17,803
I'll pick you up here at 1 0.

365
00:36:49,042 --> 00:36:49,543
Bone Saw! Bone Saw! Bone Saw!

366
00:36:49,543 --> 00:36:51,044
Bone Saw! Bone Saw! Bone Saw!

367
00:36:51,044 --> 00:36:51,712
Bone Saw! Bone Saw! Bone Saw!

368
00:36:51,712 --> 00:36:54,882
Bone Saw! Bone Saw! Bone Saw!

369
00:36:59,595 --> 00:37:03,640
- One, two, three. That's it!
- Who's the man?

370
00:37:07,769 --> 00:37:09,980
Ladies and gentlemen...

371
00:37:10,147 --> 00:37:14,693
...give it up for Bone Saw McGraw.

372
00:37:17,779 --> 00:37:21,450
For $3000...

373
00:37:21,617 --> 00:37:25,245
...is there no one here man enough
to stay in the ring...

374
00:37:25,412 --> 00:37:30,125
...for three minutes
with this titan of testosterone?

375
00:37:32,711 --> 00:37:34,796
Who?

376
00:37:35,047 --> 00:37:36,924
I know who.

377
00:37:37,132 --> 00:37:41,929
The Flying Dutchman!

378
00:37:42,262 --> 00:37:43,722
Next.

379
00:37:44,556 --> 00:37:47,851
There's no featherweight
division here smallfry. Next.

380
00:37:48,018 --> 00:37:49,853
No, no. Sign me up.

381
00:37:50,270 --> 00:37:53,690
Okay. You understand the NYWL
is not responsible...

382
00:37:53,899 --> 00:37:58,175
...for any injury you may and probably
will sustain while participating in said event

383
00:37:58,278 --> 00:38:01,406
and you are indeed participating of your own free will?
- Yes.

384
00:38:01,573 --> 00:38:05,619
Down the hall to the ramp.
May God be with you. Next.

385
00:38:08,205 --> 00:38:10,457
Told you! Told you!

386
00:38:10,666 --> 00:38:12,459
Winner!

387
00:38:12,668 --> 00:38:13,877
Next victim!

388
00:38:15,754 --> 00:38:18,632
Are you ready for more?

389
00:38:19,758 --> 00:38:23,345
Bone Saw is ready!

390
00:38:25,764 --> 00:38:30,435
Will the next victim please
enter the arena at this time?

391
00:38:30,644 --> 00:38:35,357
If he can withstand just three minutes
in the cage with Bone Saw McGraw...

392
00:38:35,607 --> 00:38:39,987
...the sum of $3000 will be paid to...

393
00:38:40,863 --> 00:38:43,866
- What's your name, kid?
- The Human Spider.

394
00:38:44,449 --> 00:38:46,827
The Human Spider? That's it.
That's the best you got?

395
00:38:46,994 --> 00:38:49,121
- Yeah.
- Oh, that sucks.

396
00:38:49,288 --> 00:38:53,792
The sum of $3000 will be paid to...

397
00:38:53,959 --> 00:38:57,212
...the terrifying, the deadly...

398
00:38:57,462 --> 00:39:00,674
...the amazing Spiderman!

399
00:39:03,051 --> 00:39:05,679
- My Name's the Human Spider.
- I don't care, get out there.

400
00:39:05,846 --> 00:39:08,891
- No, he got my name wrong.
- Get out there, moron.

401
00:39:11,393 --> 00:39:13,937
Bone Saw will eat you up
and spit you out, little man.

402
00:39:14,188 --> 00:39:16,231
I hope you brought your mommy.

403
00:39:16,398 --> 00:39:20,652
- We'll break you!
- You'll need someone to cry to.

404
00:39:21,195 --> 00:39:26,325
I'm gonna rip all eight of your
feeble legs off one by one.

405
00:39:26,825 --> 00:39:28,869
Oh, my God!

406
00:39:29,077 --> 00:39:30,704
Oh, my legs!

407
00:39:30,871 --> 00:39:33,499
Oh, God. I can't feel my legs.

408
00:39:33,665 --> 00:39:35,667
Kill! Kill! Kill!

409
00:39:43,926 --> 00:39:45,427
Cage! Cage! Cage!

410
00:39:45,594 --> 00:39:46,803
Cage!

411
00:39:56,146 --> 00:39:57,606
Hello? Guys?

412
00:39:58,649 --> 00:40:03,612
Will the guards please lock
the cage doors at this time?

413
00:40:04,321 --> 00:40:08,617
Hey listen! This is some kind of mistake.
I didn't sign up for a cage match!

414
00:40:09,785 --> 00:40:12,287
Unlock the thing! Take the chain off!

415
00:40:12,496 --> 00:40:14,289
Hey, freak show!

416
00:40:14,498 --> 00:40:17,125
You're going nowhere.

417
00:40:17,292 --> 00:40:19,670
I got you for three minutes.

418
00:40:19,837 --> 00:40:22,130
Three minutes of playtime.

419
00:40:28,762 --> 00:40:32,224
- What are you doing up there?
- Staying away from you.

420
00:40:32,432 --> 00:40:36,478
That's a cute outfit.
Did your husband give it to you?

421
00:40:42,151 --> 00:40:43,694
Finish him off!

422
00:40:50,868 --> 00:40:52,411
Smash him!

423
00:40:59,585 --> 00:41:01,336
- Hit him!
- Harder!

424
00:41:03,338 --> 00:41:05,674
Kick his spider ass!

425
00:41:07,676 --> 00:41:08,844
Hit him!

426
00:41:22,274 --> 00:41:24,067
One, two, three!

427
00:41:24,276 --> 00:41:27,070
That's it! That's it!
Winner!

428
00:41:27,237 --> 00:41:32,326
Ladies and gentlemen, give it up
for the new champion, Spiderman!

429
00:41:49,718 --> 00:41:51,386
Now get out of here.

430
00:41:53,013 --> 00:41:55,849
A hundred bucks? The ad said 3000.

431
00:41:56,058 --> 00:41:58,435
Well, check it again, webhead.

432
00:41:58,602 --> 00:42:02,481
It said three grand for three minutes.
You pinned him in two.

433
00:42:02,689 --> 00:42:06,068
For that, I give you 100.
You're lucky to get that.

434
00:42:06,235 --> 00:42:07,611
I need that money.

435
00:42:08,070 --> 00:42:11,156
I missed the part
where that's my problem.

436
00:42:19,248 --> 00:42:22,584
- Hey, what the hell...?
- Put the money in the bag.

437
00:42:24,419 --> 00:42:25,754
Hurry up!

438
00:42:32,094 --> 00:42:34,179
Hey! He stole the gate!

439
00:42:34,346 --> 00:42:36,306
Stop that guy!

440
00:42:36,598 --> 00:42:39,142
Stop him! He's got my money!

441
00:42:39,351 --> 00:42:40,602
Thanks.

442
00:42:41,854 --> 00:42:44,231
What the hell's the matter with you,
you let him go!

443
00:42:44,398 --> 00:42:46,650
Cut him off and call the cops!

444
00:42:46,817 --> 00:42:50,863
You could've taken that guy apart.
Now he's going to get away with my money.

445
00:42:51,029 --> 00:42:54,408
I missed the part
where that's my problem.

446
00:43:12,801 --> 00:43:16,227
- You gotta get back.
- I can't see. What happened?

447
00:43:16,972 --> 00:43:18,348
Old dude, man.

448
00:43:18,557 --> 00:43:22,728
Come on, folks. Keep moving, please.
Keep moving. Let's go!

449
00:43:22,895 --> 00:43:25,731
- What happened?
- Someone got hurt.

450
00:43:28,108 --> 00:43:31,320
- Excuse me. Excuse me. Excuse me.
- Stay back.

451
00:43:31,820 --> 00:43:33,655
- Stay back!
- That's my uncle!

452
00:43:35,824 --> 00:43:38,452
- What happened?
- Carjacker. He's been shot.

453
00:43:38,577 --> 00:43:42,122
We just called the paramedics.
They're on their way.

454
00:43:42,331 --> 00:43:43,707
Uncle Ben?

455
00:43:44,625 --> 00:43:46,126
Uncle Ben.

456
00:43:49,880 --> 00:43:51,215
Uncle Ben?

457
00:43:54,843 --> 00:43:56,345
Peter.

458
00:43:57,221 --> 00:43:59,014
I'm here, Uncle Ben.

459
00:44:04,645 --> 00:44:05,854
Peter.

460
00:44:27,835 --> 00:44:30,879
They got the shooter.
He's headed south on Fifth.

461
00:44:31,088 --> 00:44:35,801
We got three cars in pursuit.
All right, folks. Come on, move back.

462
00:47:12,916 --> 00:47:14,835
Get a unit to the rear!

463
00:47:17,880 --> 00:47:19,423
I got the back!

464
00:47:32,352 --> 00:47:33,687
Who's there?

465
00:47:59,963 --> 00:48:03,091
Don't hurt me. Just give me a chance.
Just give me a chance!

466
00:48:03,258 --> 00:48:07,763
What about my uncle?
Did you give him a chance? Did you?

467
00:48:07,930 --> 00:48:09,431
Answer me!

468
00:48:12,768 --> 00:48:14,102
Stop that guy!

469
00:48:19,566 --> 00:48:21,276
Thanks.

470
00:48:31,161 --> 00:48:32,287
See you.

471
00:48:53,976 --> 00:48:57,437
Freeze! We've got the place
completely surrounded.

472
00:49:39,938 --> 00:49:42,608
Oh, no. My God.

473
00:49:44,485 --> 00:49:48,197
Oh, no.
Oh, my God. No!

474
00:49:56,538 --> 00:49:59,500
- Good evening.
- General. Good to see you.

475
00:50:00,292 --> 00:50:03,170
Our exoskeleton's got
real firepower, General Slocum.

476
00:50:03,337 --> 00:50:08,759
Well, if it does what you say it can,
I'll sign that contract tomorrow.

477
00:50:09,468 --> 00:50:13,013
- He's clear! Go!
- I assume you're confident about this test.

478
00:50:13,180 --> 00:50:15,474
Absolutely, Captain Curtis is our top pilot.

479
00:50:16,225 --> 00:50:18,977
Now, what about
your commitment to OSCORP?

480
00:50:19,144 --> 00:50:23,065
Nothing would please me more
than to put Norman Osborn out of business.

481
00:50:25,400 --> 00:50:28,445
Preflight complete. Mark.

482
00:50:32,574 --> 00:50:35,202
We are picking up an
unidentified object closing fast.

483
00:50:35,369 --> 00:50:36,453
What the hell is that?

484
00:50:36,620 --> 00:50:38,121
Can you see anything?

485
00:50:38,580 --> 00:50:39,957
Oh, my God!

486
00:50:50,259 --> 00:50:53,095
- Say "chess."
- Chess!

487
00:50:53,595 --> 00:50:55,472
Peter!

488
00:50:55,681 --> 00:51:00,227
Darling, I'm so proud of you.
You looked so handsome up there.

489
00:51:00,394 --> 00:51:03,897
Pete. Good news. My Father got the place in
New York so we're all set this Friday.

490
00:51:04,064 --> 00:51:05,607
- Oh that's great!
- You made it.

491
00:51:08,360 --> 00:51:11,697
It's not the first time
I've been proven wrong.

492
00:51:13,115 --> 00:51:15,284
- Congratulations.
- Thanks, Dad.

493
00:51:15,701 --> 00:51:18,287
Peter, the science award.
That's terrific.

494
00:51:18,704 --> 00:51:19,997
Yeah.

495
00:51:22,958 --> 00:51:26,336
I know this has been
a difficult time for you...

496
00:51:26,503 --> 00:51:29,756
...but I want you to try
to enjoy this day.

497
00:51:29,965 --> 00:51:31,508
Commencement:

498
00:51:31,675 --> 00:51:35,804
The end of one thing,
the start of something new.

499
00:51:37,639 --> 00:51:41,310
I don't want to be with you anymore.
Here's your ring.

500
00:51:42,186 --> 00:51:44,062
You know what? Whatever.

501
00:51:44,605 --> 00:51:46,064
Your loss.

502
00:51:46,773 --> 00:51:50,319
You're like a brother to Harry.
That makes you family.

503
00:51:50,486 --> 00:51:54,323
And if you ever need anything,
just give me a call.

504
00:52:08,212 --> 00:52:10,464
Can I fix you something?

505
00:52:10,631 --> 00:52:12,132
No, thanks.

506
00:52:56,885 --> 00:52:59,096
I missed him a lot today.

507
00:53:01,682 --> 00:53:03,183
I know.

508
00:53:04,935 --> 00:53:06,770
I miss him too.

509
00:53:08,522 --> 00:53:10,858
But he was there.

510
00:53:14,027 --> 00:53:19,241
I can't help thinking about
the last thing I said to him.

511
00:53:19,533 --> 00:53:24,454
He tried to tell me something important,
and I threw it in his face.

512
00:53:26,206 --> 00:53:28,292
You loved him...

513
00:53:29,960 --> 00:53:32,212
...and he loved you.

514
00:53:33,088 --> 00:53:36,758
He never doubted
the man you'd grow into.

515
00:53:36,925 --> 00:53:40,387
How you were meant for great things.

516
00:53:40,929 --> 00:53:43,265
You won't disappoint him.

517
00:54:16,798 --> 00:54:20,969
With great power
comes great responsibility.

518
00:54:21,136 --> 00:54:24,348
Remember that, Pete. Remember that.

519
00:54:34,358 --> 00:54:35,609
Hurry up!

520
00:54:47,996 --> 00:54:51,750
This is not a man. My brother saw him building a
nest in the Lincoln Center fountain.

521
00:54:51,917 --> 00:54:55,128
They think he's human.
They think he's a man. Could be a woman.

522
00:54:59,216 --> 00:55:01,969
Bobby. Get a load of this!

523
00:55:05,138 --> 00:55:09,393
He throws up his hands, ropes come out, and
he climbs up the ropes like a spider web.

524
00:55:09,685 --> 00:55:13,814
I see the web and it's a signature,
and I know Spiderman was here.

525
00:55:13,981 --> 00:55:16,608
The guy protects us, you know
protects the people.

526
00:55:16,775 --> 00:55:19,528
Some kind of freakyloo or something.
Wakadoo.

527
00:55:19,695 --> 00:55:21,738
He stinks and I don't like him.

528
00:55:22,447 --> 00:55:24,032
Don't move, lady!

529
00:55:32,124 --> 00:55:34,877
Guy with eight hands. Sounds hot.

530
00:55:35,085 --> 00:55:37,212
Those tights and that tight little...

531
00:55:37,379 --> 00:55:40,716
Dresses like a spider
He looks like a bug

532
00:55:40,924 --> 00:55:44,678
But we should all just give him
One big hug

533
00:55:44,887 --> 00:55:49,474
Look out
Here comes the Spiderman

534
00:55:53,145 --> 00:55:56,899
"Who is Spiderman?"
He's a criminal, that's who he is.

535
00:55:57,065 --> 00:56:00,865
A vigilante, a public menace.
Why's he on my front page?

536
00:56:01,069 --> 00:56:03,493
Mr. Jameson your wife is on line one
she needs to know if--

537
00:56:03,572 --> 00:56:06,569
- Mr. Jameson there's a page six problem.
-We have a page one problem, shut up.

538
00:56:06,909 --> 00:56:08,452
- Well?
- He's news.

539
00:56:08,660 --> 00:56:11,163
- These are really important clients they can't wait.
- They're about to.

540
00:56:11,330 --> 00:56:15,334
- He pulled six people off that subway car.
- Sure from a wreck he probably caused.

541
00:56:15,501 --> 00:56:19,671
Something goes wrong and this creepy-crawler is there.
Look at that, he's fleeing the scene.  What's that tell you?

542
00:56:19,838 --> 00:56:23,800
He's not fleeing, he's probably going to
save somebody else. He's a hero!

543
00:56:23,967 --> 00:56:26,762
Then why's he wear a mask, hmm?
What's he got to hide?

544
00:56:26,929 --> 00:56:29,973
She needs to know
if you want chintz or chenille in the dining room.

545
00:56:30,140 --> 00:56:32,601
- Whichever's cheaper.
- Mr. Jameson it's like this,

546
00:56:32,768 --> 00:56:36,605
We double-booked page six. See so both
Macy's and Conway's have three-quarters of the same page.

547
00:56:36,772 --> 00:56:39,942
- We sold out four printings.
- Sold out?

548
00:56:40,108 --> 00:56:41,318
Every copy.

549
00:56:42,110 --> 00:56:45,697
Tomorrow morning. Spiderman. Page one with a decent
picture this time. Move Conway to page seven.

550
00:56:45,864 --> 00:56:48,784
- That's a problem.
- Make it page eight and give 'em 10 percent off.
No make it 5 percent.

551
00:56:48,951 --> 00:56:50,619
- That can't be done.
- Get outta here!

552
00:56:50,786 --> 00:56:55,666
Problem is we don't have a decent picture.
Eddie's been on it for weeks, we can barely get a glimpse of him.

553
00:56:55,833 --> 00:56:57,960
Aw, what is he, shy?

554
00:56:58,126 --> 00:57:02,130
We can get a picture of Julia Roberts in a thong
we can certainly get a picture of this weirdo.

555
00:57:02,297 --> 00:57:05,717
Put an ad on the front page.
"Cash money for a picture of Spiderman"

556
00:57:05,884 --> 00:57:09,346
He doesn't want to be famous?
I'll make him infamous!

557
00:57:21,817 --> 00:57:23,235
Buzz off.

558
00:57:23,944 --> 00:57:26,905
- M.J., it's me, Peter.
- Hi!

559
00:57:28,615 --> 00:57:33,495
- What are you doing around here?
- I'm begging for a job. How about you?

560
00:57:33,996 --> 00:57:37,708
- I'm headed to an audition.
- An audition? So you're acting now?

561
00:57:37,875 --> 00:57:38,917
Yeah.

562
00:57:39,126 --> 00:57:43,005
I work steady.
In fact, I just got off a job.

563
00:57:43,172 --> 00:57:44,339
That's great MJ.

564
00:57:44,923 --> 00:57:48,135
- You're doing it. Living your dream.
- Hey counter girl!

565
00:57:48,302 --> 00:57:49,928
Your drawer was short six dollars!

566
00:57:50,095 --> 00:57:52,723
Next time that happens,
I'm gonna take it outta your cheque!

567
00:57:53,807 --> 00:57:57,603
Excuse me, Miss Watson?
I'm talking to you! Hey!

568
00:57:57,811 --> 00:58:00,105
Yes, Enrique! Okay? I get you.

569
00:58:00,272 --> 00:58:04,401
It better not happen no more, hear me?.
Don't roll your eyes at me.

570
00:58:11,366 --> 00:58:13,076
Some dream, huh?

571
00:58:13,952 --> 00:58:16,580
It's nothing to be
embarrassed about.

572
00:58:16,747 --> 00:58:19,541
- Don't tell Harry.
- Don't tell Harry?

573
00:58:19,958 --> 00:58:24,546
Don't you guys live together?
We're going out. Didn't he tell you?

574
00:58:24,963 --> 00:58:26,548
Oh, yeah. Right.

575
00:58:26,798 --> 00:58:29,885
I think he'd hate the idea
of my waiting tables.

576
00:58:30,052 --> 00:58:34,473
- He'd think it was low or something.
- It's not low. You have a job.

577
00:58:34,806 --> 00:58:39,144
You know, Harry doesn't live on
a little place I like to call Earth.

578
00:58:40,646 --> 00:58:42,564
No, I guess not.

579
00:58:47,569 --> 00:58:49,154
Thanks, Pete.

580
00:58:50,572 --> 00:58:52,491
We should catch up sometime.

581
00:58:56,703 --> 00:58:59,248
Let's get some lunch some evening.

582
00:59:00,499 --> 00:59:05,003
I'll come by and have some of your
Moondance coffee some day.

583
00:59:05,212 --> 00:59:07,923
- And I won't tell Harry.
- No, don't tell Harry.

584
00:59:08,090 --> 00:59:09,341
I won't.

585
00:59:11,510 --> 00:59:13,262
I won't tell Harry.

586
00:59:24,565 --> 00:59:27,025
Timing's perfect. Hey.

587
00:59:27,234 --> 00:59:30,529
Five new contracts. It'll be great.

588
00:59:32,656 --> 00:59:35,367
Stormin' Norman's making his weekly inspection.

589
00:59:36,160 --> 00:59:38,412
Spent half of it on the phone.

590
00:59:38,996 --> 00:59:43,709
Look, man, I'm glad you're here.
I need your help. I'm really lost here.

591
00:59:44,543 --> 00:59:45,836
Are you all right?

592
00:59:47,171 --> 00:59:51,717
You look like you just got
second place in the science fair.

593
00:59:53,010 --> 00:59:55,971
I was late for work
and Dr. Connors fired me.

594
00:59:56,138 --> 00:59:57,681
You were late again?

595
00:59:58,307 --> 01:00:02,269
I don't get it.
Where do you go all the time?

596
01:00:02,436 --> 01:00:03,687
Around.

597
01:00:03,854 --> 01:00:05,564
Peter Parker.

598
01:00:05,898 --> 01:00:08,400
- Maybe you'll tell me who she is.
- Who's that?

599
01:00:08,567 --> 01:00:11,653
- This mystery girl Harry's been dating.
- Dad.

600
01:00:12,029 --> 01:00:13,697
- When do I get to meet her?
- Dad!

601
01:00:13,864 --> 01:00:17,159
Well, sorry.
Harry hasn't mentioned her.

602
01:00:20,037 --> 01:00:23,290
Pete, you're probably looking
for a job now, right?

603
01:00:23,499 --> 01:00:26,335
Dad, maybe you can help him out.

604
01:00:26,502 --> 01:00:30,839
- I appreciate it, but I'll be fine.
- It's no problem.  I'll make a few calls.

605
01:00:31,006 --> 01:00:35,302
I couldn't accept it. I'd like to earn
what I get. I can find my own work.

606
01:00:35,511 --> 01:00:37,137
I respect that.

607
01:00:37,846 --> 01:00:39,973
You want to make it on your own steam.

608
01:00:40,641 --> 01:00:41,975
That's great.

609
01:00:42,851 --> 01:00:45,187
What other skills do you have Parker?

610
01:00:45,395 --> 01:00:47,523
I was thinking of something in photography.

611
01:00:50,484 --> 01:00:51,735
Hello.

612
01:00:53,654 --> 01:00:55,948
Let's go! Move it!

613
01:00:57,115 --> 01:00:58,784
Watch the street!

614
01:01:14,216 --> 01:01:15,592
Cheese!

615
01:01:24,518 --> 01:01:25,811
They're crap.

616
01:01:26,019 --> 01:01:28,981
Crap, crap. Megacrap.

617
01:01:29,189 --> 01:01:32,359
- I'll give you $200.
- That seems a little low.

618
01:01:32,568 --> 01:01:34,319
Take them somewhere else then.

619
01:01:34,736 --> 01:01:38,824
- Sir your wife said that tile you want in the foyer is out of stock.
- Tell her we'll just put a rug there.

620
01:01:39,199 --> 01:01:41,160
Sit down. Give me that.

621
01:01:42,744 --> 01:01:45,289
I'll give you 300.
That's a standard freelance fee.

622
01:01:45,455 --> 01:01:47,791
- Tear up page one. Run that photo instead.
- Headline?

623
01:01:48,083 --> 01:01:51,295
"Spiderman, Hero or Menace?
Exclusive Daily Bugle Photos."

624
01:01:51,461 --> 01:01:55,081
- Menace? He was protecting that--
- Tell you what, Atticus you take the pictures

625
01:01:55,116 --> 01:01:57,467
I'll make up the headlines, ok? all right?
That ok with you.

626
01:01:57,634 --> 01:01:59,636
- Yes, sir.
- Goody.

627
01:02:00,095 --> 01:02:03,599
Give this to the girl up front.
She'll see you get paid.

628
01:02:04,057 --> 01:02:06,852
- I'd like a job, sir.
- No jobs. Freelance.

629
01:02:07,060 --> 01:02:08,687
Best thing in the world for a kid your age.

630
01:02:08,896 --> 01:02:13,192
Bring me some more shots of that newspaper selling clown,
maybe I'll take 'em off your hands.

631
01:02:13,400 --> 01:02:16,361
But I never said you have a job. Meat.

632
01:02:16,528 --> 01:02:19,240
I'll send you a box of Christmas
meat. Best I can do. Get outta here.

633
01:02:19,727 --> 01:02:20,770
Bring me more photos.

634
01:02:22,409 --> 01:02:23,619
- Hi.
- Hi.

635
01:02:23,827 --> 01:02:27,247
Mr. Jameson told me
to give that to you.

636
01:02:28,332 --> 01:02:31,460
- Welcome to the Daily Bugle.
- Thank you.

637
01:02:32,002 --> 01:02:33,378
I'm Peter Parker.

638
01:02:35,881 --> 01:02:38,050
I'm a photographer.

639
01:02:38,842 --> 01:02:41,386
Yes. I can see that.

640
01:02:49,102 --> 01:02:50,938
As of today...

641
01:02:51,104 --> 01:02:55,108
...OSCORP Industries has surpassed
Quest Aerospace...

642
01:02:55,359 --> 01:02:59,780
...as the principal supplier
to the United States military.

643
01:02:59,947 --> 01:03:02,783
In short, ladies and gentlemen
of the board...

644
01:03:02,950 --> 01:03:06,119
...costs are down, revenues are up...

645
01:03:06,370 --> 01:03:09,206
...and our stock
has never been higher.

646
01:03:09,373 --> 01:03:13,794
Wonderful news, Norman. Woderful.
In fact, it's the reason for selling the company.

647
01:03:14,628 --> 01:03:15,879
What?

648
01:03:16,088 --> 01:03:21,218
Yes, Quest Aerospace is recapitalizing
in the wake of the bombing. Expanding.

649
01:03:21,468 --> 01:03:24,221
They made a tender offer
we can't ignore.

650
01:03:24,388 --> 01:03:25,556
Why wasn't I told?

651
01:03:25,722 --> 01:03:29,810
The last thing they want is a power struggle
with entrenched management.

652
01:03:30,102 --> 01:03:32,396
The deal is off if you come with it.

653
01:03:32,563 --> 01:03:35,983
The board expects your resignation
in 30 days.

654
01:03:36,191 --> 01:03:38,152
You can't do this to me.

655
01:03:41,321 --> 01:03:43,615
I started this company.

656
01:03:44,658 --> 01:03:47,077
You know how much I sacrificed?!

657
01:03:50,914 --> 01:03:56,378
- Oh, Max. Please.
- Norman, the board is unanimous.

658
01:03:56,920 --> 01:04:00,924
We're announcing the sale
after the World Unity Festival.

659
01:04:01,091 --> 01:04:02,593
I'm sorry.

660
01:04:03,594 --> 01:04:05,721
You're out, Norman.

661
01:04:15,606 --> 01:04:17,107
Am I?

662
01:04:20,903 --> 01:04:21,570
Welcome to OSCORP Industries
Unity Day Festival.

663
01:04:21,570 --> 01:04:24,072
Welcome to OSCORP Industries
Unity Day Festival.

664
01:04:24,072 --> 01:04:27,068
Let's hear it for Macy Gray.

665
01:05:04,238 --> 01:05:07,783
M.J., why didn't you wear
the black dress?

666
01:05:08,826 --> 01:05:12,496
Just, I wanted to impress my father.
He loves black.

667
01:05:12,663 --> 01:05:17,209
Well, maybe he'll be impressed
no matter what. You think I'm pretty.

668
01:05:17,751 --> 01:05:20,128
I think you're beautiful.

669
01:05:32,933 --> 01:05:36,186
MJ would you do me a favour?
I forgot my drink inside.

670
01:05:46,405 --> 01:05:48,532
- Oh, hi, Mr. Fargas.
- Oh, Harry.

671
01:05:49,616 --> 01:05:54,788
- Have you seen my father around?
- Well, I'm not sure if he's coming today.

672
01:06:06,800 --> 01:06:09,303
- What is that?
- Must be new this year.

673
01:06:14,183 --> 01:06:15,476
What is that?

674
01:06:15,642 --> 01:06:17,561
That's our glider!

675
01:06:27,946 --> 01:06:29,406
What the hell was that?

676
01:06:57,810 --> 01:06:59,228
Code three! Code three!

677
01:07:15,244 --> 01:07:17,412
- Oh, my God! Harry!
- M.J.!

678
01:07:23,377 --> 01:07:26,839
Harry! Help me! Harry!

679
01:07:32,803 --> 01:07:34,555
Out, am I?

680
01:07:39,101 --> 01:07:42,312
- Mary Jane!
- Harry!

681
01:07:44,314 --> 01:07:46,191
Hello, my dear.

682
01:07:47,192 --> 01:07:49,027
It's Spiderman!

683
01:08:00,539 --> 01:08:02,499
- Come on. Move, kid.
- Billy!

684
01:08:06,003 --> 01:08:08,338
Somebody help him!

685
01:08:08,547 --> 01:08:10,591
No!

686
01:08:11,592 --> 01:08:13,135
Mommy!

687
01:08:15,137 --> 01:08:17,097
- Hold it right there!
- I surrender.

688
01:08:17,681 --> 01:08:20,184
- Oh, boy.
- Hold it right there!

689
01:08:25,981 --> 01:08:27,232
Impressive.

690
01:08:51,507 --> 01:08:54,968
- Mary Jane!
- Help! Someone please help me!

691
01:09:20,327 --> 01:09:21,370
Hold on!

692
01:09:22,996 --> 01:09:24,039
Watch out!

693
01:09:33,173 --> 01:09:36,969
We'll meet again, Spiderman!

694
01:09:38,672 --> 01:09:40,033
Hold on Mary Jane!

695
01:10:22,473 --> 01:10:25,142
Well, beats taking the subway.

696
01:10:25,350 --> 01:10:28,604
Don't mind us.
She just needs to use the elevator.

697
01:10:28,770 --> 01:10:29,897
Wait.

698
01:10:30,063 --> 01:10:31,315
Who are you?

699
01:10:31,482 --> 01:10:34,067
- You know who I am.
- I do?

700
01:10:34,276 --> 01:10:36,904
Your friendly neighborhood Spiderman.

701
01:10:48,624 --> 01:10:52,503
Incredible?
What do you mean he's incredible?

702
01:10:53,670 --> 01:10:57,341
No. All right, wait.
Stay there. I'm going to come over.

703
01:10:58,008 --> 01:10:59,676
No, I'm gonna come...

704
01:11:00,010 --> 01:11:03,430
All right. Fine.
Will you call me in the morning?

705
01:11:03,639 --> 01:11:06,600
And we'll go and have breakfast and...

706
01:11:06,767 --> 01:11:09,061
...I want to buy you something.

707
01:11:09,228 --> 01:11:12,564
Because I want to.
It'll make you feel better.

708
01:11:13,607 --> 01:11:17,277
Okay. And what do you mean,
incredible?

709
01:11:20,113 --> 01:11:22,491
All right. I'm sorry. Sleep tight.

710
01:11:22,658 --> 01:11:24,409
Don't let the bedbugs...

711
01:11:30,082 --> 01:11:33,126
She's all right.
She's just a little rattled.

712
01:11:34,837 --> 01:11:38,465
Look, Pete, I should have
told you about us.

713
01:11:39,800 --> 01:11:42,469
But you should know
I'm crazy about her.

714
01:11:42,636 --> 01:11:45,681
It's just, you know,
you never made a move.

715
01:11:46,765 --> 01:11:48,267
You're right.

716
01:11:49,184 --> 01:11:50,686
I didn't.

717
01:11:54,690 --> 01:11:57,109
I'm gonna get some rest.

718
01:11:58,360 --> 01:12:00,612
I'm gonna stay up for a while.

719
01:12:01,697 --> 01:12:03,448
What was that thing?

720
01:12:04,032 --> 01:12:05,367
I don't know.

721
01:12:06,785 --> 01:12:10,164
Whatever it is,
somebody has to stop it.

722
01:12:26,054 --> 01:12:27,556
Somebody there?

723
01:12:27,556 --> 01:12:28,348
Somebody.

724
01:12:28,348 --> 01:12:30,017
Somebody.

725
01:12:31,351 --> 01:12:32,895
Who said that?

726
01:12:33,562 --> 01:12:36,899
Don't play the innocent with me.

727
01:12:39,359 --> 01:12:42,029
You've known all along.

728
01:12:46,033 --> 01:12:47,409
Where are you?

729
01:12:47,576 --> 01:12:51,622
Follow the cold shiver
running down your spine.

730
01:12:58,504 --> 01:13:00,339
I'm right here.

731
01:13:02,090 --> 01:13:04,092
I don't understand.

732
01:13:05,093 --> 01:13:08,263
Did you think it was coincidence?

733
01:13:08,514 --> 01:13:12,059
So many good things,
all happening for you.

734
01:13:12,226 --> 01:13:15,896
All for you. Norman.

735
01:13:18,440 --> 01:13:19,858
What do you want?

736
01:13:20,400 --> 01:13:22,444
To say what you won't.

737
01:13:22,736 --> 01:13:25,280
To do what you can't.

738
01:13:25,447 --> 01:13:30,035
To remove those in your way.

739
01:13:33,997 --> 01:13:35,958
The board members.

740
01:13:37,251 --> 01:13:38,627
You killed them.

741
01:13:38,794 --> 01:13:40,337
We killed them.

742
01:13:40,671 --> 01:13:41,713
We?

743
01:13:41,922 --> 01:13:43,465
Remember?

744
01:13:43,632 --> 01:13:46,301
Your little accident
in the laboratory.

745
01:13:48,178 --> 01:13:49,972
The performance enhancers.

746
01:13:50,139 --> 01:13:55,435
Bingo. Me!
Your greatest creation.

747
01:13:55,644 --> 01:13:59,439
Bringing you
what you've always wanted:

748
01:13:59,606 --> 01:14:02,484
Power beyond your wildest dreams.

749
01:14:02,651 --> 01:14:05,154
And it's only the beginning.

750
01:14:06,655 --> 01:14:10,993
There's only one who can stop us.

751
01:14:11,785 --> 01:14:15,164
Or imagine if he joined us.

752
01:14:19,960 --> 01:14:23,172
Spiderman. And the Green Goblin.

753
01:14:23,422 --> 01:14:26,675
The Green Goblin. You like that?
Made it up myself.

754
01:14:26,842 --> 01:14:29,845
- These weirdo's all gotta have a name now.
- Mr. Jameson Spiderman...

755
01:14:30,012 --> 01:14:31,680
- Hoffman!
- Yeah?

756
01:14:32,890 --> 01:14:36,643
Call the patent office, copyright the name Green Goblin,
I want a quarter every time somebody says it.

757
01:14:36,852 --> 01:14:39,146
How about "Green Meanie"?

758
01:14:39,313 --> 01:14:42,191
Spiderman wasn't attacking the city he was 
trying to save it. That's slander.

759
01:14:42,357 --> 01:14:44,693
It is not. I resent that.

760
01:14:44,943 --> 01:14:47,696
Slander is spoken.
In print, it's libel.

761
01:14:47,863 --> 01:14:49,531
You don't trust anybody, that's your problem.

762
01:14:49,990 --> 01:14:51,742
I trust my barber.

763
01:14:52,576 --> 01:14:54,077
What are you his lawyer? Get out of here!

764
01:14:54,286 --> 01:14:59,041
Let him sue. Get rich like a normal
person. That's what made this country...

765
01:15:06,548 --> 01:15:09,676
Jameson, you slime.

766
01:15:09,885 --> 01:15:13,180
Who's the photographer who takes the
pictures of Spiderman?

767
01:15:13,388 --> 01:15:16,308
- I don't know who he is.  His stuff comes in the mail.
- Liar!

768
01:15:16,475 --> 01:15:19,478
- I swear.
- He's the one who can bring me to him.

769
01:15:19,645 --> 01:15:22,564
- I don't know who he is.
- You are useless.

770
01:15:22,773 --> 01:15:25,025
Set him down, tough guy.

771
01:15:25,275 --> 01:15:29,863
- Speak of the devil.
- Spiderman! I knew you two were in this together.

772
01:15:30,072 --> 01:15:32,658
Hey, kiddo, let Mom and Dad
talk for a minute, will you?.

773
01:15:32,866 --> 01:15:35,327
Sleep...

774
01:15:49,800 --> 01:15:53,804
Wake up, little spider. Wake up.

775
01:15:53,971 --> 01:15:58,392
No, you're not dead yet.

776
01:15:58,600 --> 01:16:00,769
Just paralyzed...

777
01:16:00,936 --> 01:16:02,896
...temporarily.

778
01:16:03,897 --> 01:16:06,984
You're an amazing creature,
Spiderman.

779
01:16:07,192 --> 01:16:09,862
You and I are not so different.

780
01:16:10,571 --> 01:16:13,907
I'm not like you. You're a murderer.

781
01:16:14,116 --> 01:16:16,994
Well, to each his own.

782
01:16:17,161 --> 01:16:20,122
I chose my path,
you chose the way of the hero.

783
01:16:20,789 --> 01:16:25,419
And they found you amusing
for a while, the people of this city.

784
01:16:25,627 --> 01:16:28,881
But the one thing they love
more than a hero...

785
01:16:29,089 --> 01:16:32,676
...is to see a hero fail,
fall, die trying.

786
01:16:32,843 --> 01:16:37,389
In spite of everything you've done for
them, eventually, they will hate you.

787
01:16:37,598 --> 01:16:38,640
Why bother?

788
01:16:38,849 --> 01:16:43,562
- Because it's right.
- Here's the real truth.

789
01:16:43,979 --> 01:16:46,982
There are eight million people
in this city.

790
01:16:47,191 --> 01:16:51,487
And those teeming masses exist
for the sole purpose...

791
01:16:51,695 --> 01:16:55,657
...of lifting the few exceptional
people onto their shoulders.

792
01:16:55,824 --> 01:16:57,242
You, me...

793
01:16:57,826 --> 01:16:59,745
...we're exceptional.

794
01:16:59,995 --> 01:17:04,666
I could squash you like a bug
right now.

795
01:17:04,875 --> 01:17:08,545
But I'm offering you a choice.
Join me.

796
01:17:08,712 --> 01:17:12,299
Imagine what we could
accomplish together.

797
01:17:12,508 --> 01:17:15,260
What we could create.

798
01:17:15,844 --> 01:17:17,846
Or we could destroy.

799
01:17:18,013 --> 01:17:21,975
Cause the deaths of countless
innocents in selfish battle...

800
01:17:22,184 --> 01:17:27,064
...again and again and again until
we're both dead. Is that what you want?

801
01:17:29,066 --> 01:17:31,944
Think about it, hero.

802
01:17:43,914 --> 01:17:49,253
In spite of everything you've done for
them, eventually, they will hate you.

803
01:17:59,596 --> 01:18:01,056
It's me again.

804
01:18:01,431 --> 01:18:02,850
How was your audition?

805
01:18:03,058 --> 01:18:06,061
- How'd you know?
- The hot line. Your mom...

806
01:18:06,228 --> 01:18:08,188
...told my aunt, told me.

807
01:18:08,647 --> 01:18:09,982
So you just came by?

808
01:18:10,190 --> 01:18:13,819
I was in the neighborhood.
Needed to see a friendly face.

809
01:18:13,986 --> 01:18:18,574
I took two buses and a cab
to get in the neighborhood, but...

810
01:18:18,824 --> 01:18:20,325
So how'd it go?

811
01:18:22,494 --> 01:18:25,080
They said I needed acting lessons.

812
01:18:25,247 --> 01:18:29,001
A soap opera told me
I needed acting lessons.

813
01:18:29,168 --> 01:18:34,506
Let me buy you a cheeseburger.
The sky's the limit, up to $7.84.

814
01:18:35,841 --> 01:18:37,926
I'd like a cheeseburger.

815
01:18:38,385 --> 01:18:41,847
Oh, but I'm going out to dinner
with Harry.

816
01:18:42,264 --> 01:18:43,682
Come with us.

817
01:18:43,849 --> 01:18:46,602
No, thanks. How's it going with...?

818
01:18:48,520 --> 01:18:51,023
Never mind.
That's none of my business.

819
01:18:51,523 --> 01:18:53,025
It's not?

820
01:18:54,443 --> 01:18:56,111
Why so interested?

821
01:18:56,778 --> 01:18:58,280
I'm not.

822
01:18:58,530 --> 01:18:59,907
You're not?

823
01:19:01,533 --> 01:19:04,286
- Well, why would I be?
- I don't know.

824
01:19:04,536 --> 01:19:06,330
Why would you be?

825
01:19:08,207 --> 01:19:10,542
I, that's a...

826
01:19:10,751 --> 01:19:12,252
I don't know.

827
01:19:14,463 --> 01:19:17,299
Sorry you won't come with us.

828
01:19:19,760 --> 01:19:21,720
I'd better run, tiger.

829
01:19:30,437 --> 01:19:32,439
Hey, check it out, man.

830
01:19:32,606 --> 01:19:34,274
Come on, man.

831
01:19:37,820 --> 01:19:41,073
Hey, where you going, baby?
Come on!

832
01:19:58,966 --> 01:20:00,425
Get off me!

833
01:20:33,709 --> 01:20:35,210
Wait!

834
01:20:40,048 --> 01:20:42,426
You have a knack
for getting in trouble.

835
01:20:42,593 --> 01:20:46,972
You have a knack for saving my life.
I think I have a superhero stalker.

836
01:20:47,181 --> 01:20:49,057
I was in the neighborhood.

837
01:20:50,934 --> 01:20:53,562
You are amazing.

838
01:20:54,521 --> 01:20:57,232
Some people don't think so.

839
01:20:58,317 --> 01:21:01,320
- But you are.
- Nice to have a fan.

840
01:21:02,070 --> 01:21:05,282
Do I get to say thank you this time?

841
01:21:06,158 --> 01:21:07,659
Wait.

842
01:22:16,645 --> 01:22:18,772
I have to get in there! My baby's in there!
My baby's in there!

843
01:22:18,939 --> 01:22:21,066
- Let me go!
- I can't let you in there, the roof's about to collapse.

844
01:22:21,233 --> 01:22:24,736
- Somebody save my baby!
- The roof's about to collapse!

845
01:22:24,945 --> 01:22:26,280
Look! Up there!

846
01:22:32,870 --> 01:22:34,705
Save my baby, please!

847
01:22:58,437 --> 01:22:59,563
No!

848
01:23:07,321 --> 01:23:11,325
- It's okay. Your baby's fine.
- Oh, my baby!

849
01:23:12,367 --> 01:23:15,287
God bless you, Spiderman.
Bless you.

850
01:23:15,496 --> 01:23:17,247
Don't let him get away!

851
01:23:17,456 --> 01:23:20,709
Hold it right there! You're under arrest.
I'm taking you in.

852
01:23:20,876 --> 01:23:24,213
Oh, my God, there's somebody
still up there!

853
01:23:25,672 --> 01:23:27,007
I'm going.

854
01:23:28,675 --> 01:23:31,720
- I'll be here when you get back.
- Not coming back chief.

855
01:23:32,137 --> 01:23:33,263
Go! Go!

856
01:23:42,189 --> 01:23:43,899
Where are you?

857
01:23:45,943 --> 01:23:47,528
Where are you?

858
01:23:52,908 --> 01:23:55,285
I'm gonna get you out of here!

859
01:23:57,871 --> 01:23:59,373
It's okay.

860
01:24:06,421 --> 01:24:09,007
You're pathetically predictable.

861
01:24:09,174 --> 01:24:11,093
Like a moth to the flame.

862
01:24:11,969 --> 01:24:14,429
What about my generous proposal?

863
01:24:15,472 --> 01:24:18,308
Are you in or are you out?

864
01:24:18,517 --> 01:24:24,439
- It's you who's out Gobby. Out of your mind.
- Wrong answer.

865
01:24:24,857 --> 01:24:26,358
Oh, great.

866
01:25:05,022 --> 01:25:07,816
No one says no to me!

867
01:25:15,157 --> 01:25:18,577
- M.J., will you stop goofing around?
- Harry, relax.

868
01:25:21,079 --> 01:25:22,331
He's here.

869
01:25:23,123 --> 01:25:24,625
Are you ready?

870
01:25:26,460 --> 01:25:29,129
Aunt May. I'm sorry I'm late.

871
01:25:29,338 --> 01:25:32,424
Work was murder.
I picked up a fruitcake.

872
01:25:32,633 --> 01:25:36,053
Thank you, Mr. Osborn.
We're so glad you could come.

873
01:25:36,303 --> 01:25:39,014
Who is this lovely young lady?

874
01:25:39,181 --> 01:25:43,477
I'd like you to meet my father Norman Osborn.
Dad, this is Mary Jane Watson.

875
01:25:43,685 --> 01:25:46,355
How do you do?
I've been looking forward to meeting you.

876
01:25:46,563 --> 01:25:50,275
- Happy Thanksgiving, sir.
- Now, where is Peter?

877
01:25:50,442 --> 01:25:52,820
He'd better remember
that cranberry sauce.

878
01:25:58,575 --> 01:26:02,162
Oh, that's weird.
I didn't know he was here.

879
01:26:05,165 --> 01:26:06,667
Peter?

880
01:26:14,716 --> 01:26:16,426
Is that you?

881
01:26:21,890 --> 01:26:26,061
How strange. There's nobody here.

882
01:26:32,526 --> 01:26:36,989
- Bit of a slob, isn't he?
- All brilliant men are.

883
01:27:09,605 --> 01:27:12,232
- Hey, everyone.
- Oh, Peter!

884
01:27:12,399 --> 01:27:14,151
Sorry I'm late. 
It's a jungle out there.

885
01:27:14,318 --> 01:27:18,238
I had to beat an old lady with a stick
to get these cranberries.

886
01:27:18,697 --> 01:27:21,533
Thank you.
Now then, everybody sit down...

887
01:27:21,700 --> 01:27:23,285
...and we can say grace.

888
01:27:26,830 --> 01:27:28,582
Here we go.

889
01:27:35,547 --> 01:27:37,883
- There we are.
- It looks delicious.

890
01:27:41,678 --> 01:27:43,972
Will you do the honors?

891
01:27:55,651 --> 01:27:58,904
Why, Peter, you're bleeding.

892
01:28:01,740 --> 01:28:07,079
Oh, yeah, I stepped off a curb and got clipped
by one of those bike messengers.

893
01:28:07,246 --> 01:28:08,789
Well, let me see.

894
01:28:08,997 --> 01:28:10,499
Oh, my goodness.

895
01:28:10,749 --> 01:28:13,168
- That looks awful.
- No, it's nothing.

896
01:28:13,335 --> 01:28:16,463
I'll get the first-aid kit.
Then we'll say grace.

897
01:28:16,672 --> 01:28:21,969
This is the boys' first Thanksgiving in this apartment
and we are going to do things properly.

898
01:28:22,928 --> 01:28:26,014
How did you say that happened?

899
01:28:26,431 --> 01:28:28,142
Bike messenger.

900
01:28:28,350 --> 01:28:30,310
Knocked me down.

901
01:28:35,691 --> 01:28:39,361
- If you'll excuse me, I've got to be going.
- Why?

902
01:28:40,279 --> 01:28:43,657
Something has come to my attention.

903
01:28:43,866 --> 01:28:45,117
Are you all right?

904
01:28:45,325 --> 01:28:48,829
I'm fine, just fine.
Thank you, Mrs. Parker. Everyone.

905
01:28:49,454 --> 01:28:51,832
- Enjoy the fruitcake.
- Dad!

906
01:28:53,056 --> 01:28:55,057
Dad, what are you doing?

907
01:28:55,691 --> 01:28:58,196
I plan this whole thing so you can meet MJ
and now you've got to leave?

908
01:28:58,231 --> 01:28:59,673
I've got to go.

909
01:29:00,007 --> 01:29:04,136
- This girl is important to me.
- Harry, please. Look at her.

910
01:29:04,344 --> 01:29:08,307
Do you think a woman like that is sniffing
around because she likes your personality?

911
01:29:08,557 --> 01:29:11,560
- What are you saying?
- Your mother was beautiful too.

912
01:29:11,727 --> 01:29:17,149
They're all beautiful until they're snarling after
your trust fund like a pack of ravening wolves.

913
01:29:17,357 --> 01:29:18,609
You're wrong about her Dad.

914
01:29:19,151 --> 01:29:22,362
A word to the not so wise about your little girlfriend,

915
01:29:22,529 --> 01:29:26,408
Do what you need to with her,
then broom her fast.

916
01:29:36,793 --> 01:29:39,338
Thanks for sticking up for me, Harry.

917
01:29:39,546 --> 01:29:42,508
- You heard?
- Everyone heard that creep.

918
01:29:42,716 --> 01:29:46,595
That creep is my father, all right
If I'm lucky I'll become half of what he is

919
01:29:46,845 --> 01:29:49,181
so just keep your mouth shut
about stuff you don't understand.

920
01:29:49,348 --> 01:29:51,016
Harry Osborn!

921
01:29:52,100 --> 01:29:54,144
I'm sorry, Aunt May.

922
01:29:57,105 --> 01:30:00,442
Spiderman is all but invincible.

923
01:30:00,609 --> 01:30:03,737
But Parker, we can destroy him.

924
01:30:03,946 --> 01:30:05,280
I can't.

925
01:30:05,447 --> 01:30:08,450
Betrayal must not be countenanced.

926
01:30:08,700 --> 01:30:10,953
Parker must be educated.

927
01:30:13,121 --> 01:30:14,414
What do I do?

928
01:30:14,623 --> 01:30:18,710
Instruct him in the matters
of loss and pain.

929
01:30:18,877 --> 01:30:21,922
Make him suffer.
Make him wish he were dead.

930
01:30:22,172 --> 01:30:23,465
Yes?

931
01:30:23,632 --> 01:30:25,551
And then grant his wish.

932
01:30:26,468 --> 01:30:27,761
But how?

933
01:30:27,970 --> 01:30:32,266
The cunning warrior attacks
neither body nor mind.

934
01:30:32,474 --> 01:30:33,642
Tell me how!

935
01:30:33,809 --> 01:30:35,978
The heart, Osborn.

936
01:30:36,228 --> 01:30:39,273
First, we attack his heart.

937
01:30:41,150 --> 01:30:44,653
Give us this day our daily bread,
and forgive us our trespasses...

938
01:30:44,862 --> 01:30:47,823
...as we forgive those
who trespass against us.

939
01:30:48,073 --> 01:30:51,910
Lead us not into temptation,
but deliver us...

940
01:30:59,668 --> 01:31:02,212
Deliver us!

941
01:31:02,421 --> 01:31:03,797
Finish it!

942
01:31:04,089 --> 01:31:08,010
- Finish it!
- From evil!

943
01:31:13,724 --> 01:31:15,893
Two milligrams IV.

944
01:31:17,686 --> 01:31:18,937
Get the BP.

945
01:31:19,354 --> 01:31:22,103
Aunt May. Is she gonna be okay?
What happened?

946
01:31:22,599 --> 01:31:25,124
Yes she's going to be ok.
Look you're going to have to leave right now.

947
01:31:25,159 --> 01:31:26,361
- What happened?
- Those eyes!

948
01:31:26,528 --> 01:31:30,616
Those horrible yellow eyes!

949
01:31:35,454 --> 01:31:37,998
He knows who I am.

950
01:32:21,959 --> 01:32:23,544
I'm sorry.

951
01:32:27,256 --> 01:32:29,716
- Will she be okay?
- She's going to be fine.

952
01:32:29,883 --> 01:32:32,553
She's been sleeping all day.

953
01:32:33,554 --> 01:32:36,306
- Thanks for coming.
- Of course.

954
01:32:40,477 --> 01:32:43,397
How are you?
You okay about the other night?

955
01:32:43,564 --> 01:32:47,276
Yeah, I'm fine. I just felt bad
about leaving Aunt May.

956
01:32:47,484 --> 01:32:50,445
- Have you talked to Harry?
- He called me.

957
01:32:50,904 --> 01:32:53,073
I haven't called him back.

958
01:32:55,159 --> 01:32:56,869
The fact is...

959
01:32:58,036 --> 01:33:00,873
...I'm in love with somebody else.
- You are?

960
01:33:01,039 --> 01:33:03,250
At least I think I am.

961
01:33:04,918 --> 01:33:07,963
- It's not the time to talk about it.
- No. Go on.

962
01:33:08,130 --> 01:33:11,383
Would I know his name, this guy?

963
01:33:11,592 --> 01:33:14,470
You'll think I'm a stupid little
girl with a crush.

964
01:33:14,636 --> 01:33:16,013
Trust me.

965
01:33:16,263 --> 01:33:17,514
It's funny.

966
01:33:19,516 --> 01:33:23,479
He's saved my life twice,
and I've never even seen his face.

967
01:33:23,645 --> 01:33:27,024
- Oh. Him.
- You're laughing at me.

968
01:33:27,232 --> 01:33:30,194
No, I understand.
He is extremely cool.

969
01:33:30,402 --> 01:33:34,698
But do you think it's true,
all the terrible things they say about him?

970
01:33:34,865 --> 01:33:37,784
No, no, not Spiderman,
not a chance in the world.

971
01:33:37,993 --> 01:33:39,620
I know him a little bit.

972
01:33:39,828 --> 01:33:42,706
I'm sort of his unofficial
photographer.

973
01:33:42,915 --> 01:33:46,043
- Has he mentioned me?
- Yeah.

974
01:33:46,376 --> 01:33:47,836
What'd he say?

975
01:33:48,420 --> 01:33:49,755
I said...

976
01:33:50,839 --> 01:33:55,135
He asked me what I thought about you.

977
01:33:56,053 --> 01:33:58,096
And what did you say?

978
01:33:58,806 --> 01:34:02,893
I said, "Spiderman."

979
01:34:03,227 --> 01:34:08,106
I said, "The great thing about M. J...

980
01:34:08,315 --> 01:34:09,858
...is...

981
01:34:10,776 --> 01:34:14,029
...when you look in her eyes...

982
01:34:16,573 --> 01:34:19,785
...and she's looking back in yours...

983
01:34:20,786 --> 01:34:23,789
...everything feels...

984
01:34:24,998 --> 01:34:26,834
...not quite normal.

985
01:34:28,085 --> 01:34:29,878
Because you feel...

986
01:34:30,420 --> 01:34:32,047
...stronger...

987
01:34:33,590 --> 01:34:37,219
...and weaker at the same time.

988
01:34:38,262 --> 01:34:40,389
You feel excited...

989
01:34:41,265 --> 01:34:43,308
...and at the same time...

990
01:34:43,934 --> 01:34:45,561
...terrified.

991
01:34:47,896 --> 01:34:52,192
The truth is, you don't know
what you feel...

992
01:34:53,610 --> 01:34:57,239
...except you know what kind of man
you want to be.

993
01:34:59,950 --> 01:35:01,827
It's as if you've...

994
01:35:02,452 --> 01:35:05,622
...reached the unreachable...

995
01:35:07,207 --> 01:35:09,918
...and you weren't ready for it."

996
01:35:13,380 --> 01:35:15,132
You said that?

997
01:35:15,924 --> 01:35:18,260
Well, something like that.

998
01:36:02,554 --> 01:36:04,056
Dad?

999
01:36:09,394 --> 01:36:11,480
Dad, is that you?

1000
01:36:18,070 --> 01:36:19,571
What is it?

1001
01:36:21,824 --> 01:36:26,829
You were right about M.J.
You're right about everything.

1002
01:36:27,830 --> 01:36:30,541
She's in love with Peter.

1003
01:36:30,833 --> 01:36:32,626
- Parker?
- Yeah.

1004
01:36:32,793 --> 01:36:35,921
And how does he feel about her?

1005
01:36:37,339 --> 01:36:39,883
He's loved her since the 4th grade.

1006
01:36:40,843 --> 01:36:46,098
He pretends like he doesn't, but
there's no one Peter cares for more.

1007
01:36:49,017 --> 01:36:50,769
I'm so sorry.

1008
01:36:53,230 --> 01:36:56,692
I haven't always been there for you,
have I?

1009
01:36:58,443 --> 01:37:01,655
You're busy. You're an important man.
I understand.

1010
01:37:01,822 --> 01:37:03,657
That's no excuse.

1011
01:37:04,658 --> 01:37:06,451
I'm proud of you.

1012
01:37:06,994 --> 01:37:11,874
I've lost sight of that somewhere.
But I'll make it up to you, Harry.

1013
01:37:12,040 --> 01:37:15,294
I'm going to rectify
certain inequities.

1014
01:37:29,433 --> 01:37:31,226
Wake up, little spider.

1015
01:37:31,393 --> 01:37:32,895
Wake up.

1016
01:37:34,229 --> 01:37:35,814
Go home, dear.

1017
01:37:36,023 --> 01:37:37,357
You look awful.

1018
01:37:37,566 --> 01:37:39,860
- And you look beautiful.
- Thank you.

1019
01:37:40,027 --> 01:37:43,363
- I don't like to leave you here.
- But I'm safe here.

1020
01:37:43,530 --> 01:37:46,241
- Can I do anything for you?
- You do too much.

1021
01:37:46,408 --> 01:37:51,955
College, a job, all this time with me.
You're not Superman, you know.

1022
01:37:52,706 --> 01:37:54,458
A smile. Finally.

1023
01:37:54,625 --> 01:37:58,962
Haven't seen one of those on your face
since Mary Jane was here.

1024
01:37:59,129 --> 01:38:01,423
Hey, you were supposed to be asleep.

1025
01:38:02,257 --> 01:38:07,012
You know, you were about 6 years old
when M.J. 's family moved in next door.

1026
01:38:07,221 --> 01:38:11,225
When she got out of the car,
and you saw her for the first time...

1027
01:38:11,433 --> 01:38:17,689
...you grabbed me and said,
"Aunt May, aunt May, is that an angel?"

1028
01:38:17,898 --> 01:38:21,443
- Gee, did I say that?
- You sure did.

1029
01:38:24,112 --> 01:38:26,865
Well, Harry's in love with her.

1030
01:38:27,074 --> 01:38:30,828
- She's still his girl.
- Well, isn't that up to her?

1031
01:38:31,036 --> 01:38:35,624
- She doesn't really know who I am.
- Because you won't let her.

1032
01:38:35,833 --> 01:38:38,961
You're so mysterious all the time.

1033
01:38:39,211 --> 01:38:41,964
Tell me, would it be so dangerous...

1034
01:38:42,172 --> 01:38:46,135
...to let Mary Jane know
how much you care?

1035
01:38:46,593 --> 01:38:49,012
Everybody else knows.

1036
01:38:51,932 --> 01:38:53,225
I'll be right back.

1037
01:38:53,934 --> 01:38:55,227
But...

1038
01:39:02,568 --> 01:39:04,570
Come on, pick up.

1039
01:39:04,736 --> 01:39:08,031
- Hey M.J.
-Hi. Sing your song at the beep.

1040
01:39:09,074 --> 01:39:11,118
M.J., it's Peter. You there?

1041
01:39:11,410 --> 01:39:14,246
Hello? You there?

1042
01:39:14,746 --> 01:39:19,251
I'm just calling to check up on you.
Will you call me when you get in?

1043
01:39:19,418 --> 01:39:20,836
All right, well...

1044
01:39:21,253 --> 01:39:22,296
Don't...

1045
01:39:23,088 --> 01:39:25,299
Don't go up any dark alleys.

1046
01:39:25,507 --> 01:39:27,009
Hello?

1047
01:39:29,428 --> 01:39:33,140
Can Spiderman come out to play?

1048
01:39:33,348 --> 01:39:35,100
Where is she?

1049
01:40:21,355 --> 01:40:23,023
- What is that?
- That's cool!

1050
01:40:23,232 --> 01:40:27,861
The itsy-bitsy spider
Went up the water spout

1051
01:40:28,028 --> 01:40:32,199
Down came the goblin
And took the spider out

1052
01:40:49,007 --> 01:40:50,759
Goblin, what have you done?

1053
01:41:33,218 --> 01:41:37,097
Spiderman!
This is why only fools are heroes.

1054
01:41:37,473 --> 01:41:39,141
Because you never know...

1055
01:41:39,308 --> 01:41:44,062
...when some lunatic will come along
with a sadistic choice:

1056
01:41:45,189 --> 01:41:47,816
Let die the woman you love...

1057
01:41:52,112 --> 01:41:57,201
...or suffer the little children.

1058
01:41:59,578 --> 01:42:02,080
- Spiderman!
- Save us!

1059
01:42:02,581 --> 01:42:04,875
Save us!

1060
01:42:05,167 --> 01:42:07,753
Make your choice, Spiderman...

1061
01:42:07,961 --> 01:42:11,340
...and see how a hero is rewarded.

1062
01:42:11,507 --> 01:42:13,592
Don't do it, Goblin!

1063
01:42:13,759 --> 01:42:16,678
We are who we choose to be.

1064
01:42:16,929 --> 01:42:19,681
- Now, choose!
- No!

1065
01:42:48,377 --> 01:42:49,962
Everybody stay still!

1066
01:42:59,471 --> 01:43:00,764
Ahoy up there!

1067
01:43:00,931 --> 01:43:03,892
We're gonna bring the barge
right under you.

1068
01:43:11,400 --> 01:43:15,529
- He's coming back!
- Listen. I need you to climb down.

1069
01:43:15,696 --> 01:43:17,197
- I can't.
- Yes, you can!

1070
01:43:22,286 --> 01:43:25,330
M.J., you can do it. You have to.

1071
01:43:25,497 --> 01:43:27,082
Trust me.

1072
01:43:28,584 --> 01:43:32,421
Hold on tight and go quickly.

1073
01:43:36,758 --> 01:43:38,802
- Hurry!
- I can't. I can't do it.

1074
01:43:39,011 --> 01:43:40,679
Hang on, Mary Jane!

1075
01:44:09,124 --> 01:44:11,752
- He's not gonna make it.
- He's gonna make it!

1076
01:44:21,637 --> 01:44:24,848
It's time to die.

1077
01:44:31,855 --> 01:44:35,692
Come on up here dumb gu
I got a little something for ya.

1078
01:44:35,859 --> 01:44:39,279
Leave Spiderman alone.
You gonna pick on a guy trying to save a bunch of kids?

1079
01:44:39,947 --> 01:44:43,450
You mess with Spidey,
you mess with New York!

1080
01:44:43,617 --> 01:44:47,162
You mess with one of us,
you mess with all of us!

1081
01:44:59,675 --> 01:45:01,468
Spiderman, watch out!

1082
01:45:33,333 --> 01:45:37,588
Misery, misery, misery.
That's what you've chosen.

1083
01:45:38,505 --> 01:45:41,133
I offered you friendship...

1084
01:45:41,300 --> 01:45:43,177
...and you spat in my face.

1085
01:46:34,269 --> 01:46:37,940
You've spun your last web, Spiderman.

1086
01:46:38,106 --> 01:46:41,443
Had you not been so selfish, your little
girlfriend's death

1087
01:46:41,610 --> 01:46:43,278
...would have been quick and painless.

1088
01:46:43,445 --> 01:46:46,865
But now that you've really
pissed me off...

1089
01:46:47,115 --> 01:46:51,995
...l'm gonna finish her
nice and slow.

1090
01:46:56,583 --> 01:46:58,627
M.J. and I...

1091
01:46:59,461 --> 01:47:02,756
...we're gonna have a hell of a time.

1092
01:47:56,560 --> 01:47:58,103
Peter, stop!

1093
01:47:58,270 --> 01:48:00,731
Stop! It's me.

1094
01:48:09,698 --> 01:48:11,200
Mr. Osborn.

1095
01:48:11,366 --> 01:48:12,910
Peter, thank God for you.

1096
01:48:13,118 --> 01:48:15,454
You killed those people
on that balcony.

1097
01:48:15,621 --> 01:48:18,665
The Goblin killed!
I had nothing to do with it!

1098
01:48:18,832 --> 01:48:20,584
Don't let him take me again.

1099
01:48:20,751 --> 01:48:22,795
I beg you. Protect me.

1100
01:48:22,961 --> 01:48:26,548
You tried to kill Aunt May.
You tried to kill Mary Jane.

1101
01:48:26,715 --> 01:48:28,217
But not you.

1102
01:48:28,884 --> 01:48:32,846
I tried to stop it.
But I couldn't stop it.

1103
01:48:33,055 --> 01:48:35,140
I would never hurt you.

1104
01:48:35,349 --> 01:48:37,267
I knew from the beginning...

1105
01:48:37,476 --> 01:48:40,395
...if anything ever happened to me...

1106
01:48:40,562 --> 01:48:42,689
...it was you I could count on.

1107
01:48:42,856 --> 01:48:46,235
You, Peter Parker, would save me,
and so you have.

1108
01:48:46,819 --> 01:48:48,654
Thank God for you.

1109
01:48:49,655 --> 01:48:51,073
Give me your hand.

1110
01:48:52,241 --> 01:48:55,661
Believe in me
as I believed in you.

1111
01:48:57,079 --> 01:48:59,873
I've been like a father to you.

1112
01:49:01,416 --> 01:49:03,085
Be a son to me now.

1113
01:49:04,878 --> 01:49:06,755
I have a father.

1114
01:49:07,506 --> 01:49:10,008
His name was Ben Parker.

1115
01:49:11,885 --> 01:49:13,345
Godspeed, Spiderman.

1116
01:49:32,281 --> 01:49:33,782
Peter.

1117
01:49:36,118 --> 01:49:37,953
Don't tell Harry.

1118
01:50:09,651 --> 01:50:11,361
What have you done?

1119
01:50:11,528 --> 01:50:13,113
What have you done?!

1120
01:50:41,266 --> 01:50:43,310
I'm so sorry, Harry.

1121
01:50:44,228 --> 01:50:47,356
I know what it's like
to lose a father.

1122
01:50:49,525 --> 01:50:52,820
I didn't lose him.
He was stolen from me.

1123
01:50:54,404 --> 01:50:56,698
One day Spiderman will pay.

1124
01:50:58,575 --> 01:51:01,703
I swear on my father's grave,
Spiderman will pay.

1125
01:51:06,708 --> 01:51:08,544
Thank God for you, Peter.

1126
01:51:09,253 --> 01:51:11,713
You're the only family I have.

1127
01:51:36,238 --> 01:51:38,532
No matter what I do...

1128
01:51:38,699 --> 01:51:41,827
... no matter how hard I try...

1129
01:51:42,411 --> 01:51:46,248
... the ones I love will always
be the ones who pay.

1130
01:51:56,967 --> 01:51:59,303
You must miss him so much.

1131
01:52:00,262 --> 01:52:03,307
It's been so hard without him.

1132
01:52:06,226 --> 01:52:09,104
There's something
I've been wanting to tell you.

1133
01:52:10,898 --> 01:52:12,691
When I was up there...

1134
01:52:13,442 --> 01:52:16,236
...and I thought I was gonna die...

1135
01:52:17,863 --> 01:52:21,700
...there was only one person
who I was thinking of.

1136
01:52:22,993 --> 01:52:26,205
And it wasn't who I thought it'd be.

1137
01:52:27,664 --> 01:52:30,083
It was you, Pete.

1138
01:52:30,959 --> 01:52:32,836
I kept thinking:

1139
01:52:33,253 --> 01:52:36,048
"I hope I make it through this...

1140
01:52:37,508 --> 01:52:41,887
...so I can see Peter Parker's face
one more time."

1141
01:52:43,263 --> 01:52:44,765
Really?

1142
01:52:45,140 --> 01:52:50,938
There's only one man
who's always been there for me...

1143
01:52:52,189 --> 01:52:54,149
...who makes me feel...

1144
01:52:54,608 --> 01:52:58,320
...like I'm more than I ever
thought I could be.

1145
01:53:00,447 --> 01:53:02,115
That I'm just...

1146
01:53:02,783 --> 01:53:04,284
...me.

1147
01:53:05,369 --> 01:53:07,287
And that's okay.

1148
01:53:09,498 --> 01:53:10,958
The truth is...

1149
01:53:13,085 --> 01:53:14,878
...I love you.

1150
01:53:17,005 --> 01:53:18,924
I love you so much, Peter.

1151
01:53:39,653 --> 01:53:44,408
All I wanted was to tell her
how much I loved her.

1152
01:53:44,575 --> 01:53:46,493
I can't...

1153
01:53:48,620 --> 01:53:50,164
You can't what?

1154
01:53:51,290 --> 01:53:52,749
Tell you...

1155
01:53:54,460 --> 01:53:58,797
...everything.
I mean, there's so much to tell.

1156
01:53:59,882 --> 01:54:03,802
Yeah. There's so much to tell.

1157
01:54:04,720 --> 01:54:06,680
I want you to know...

1158
01:54:07,097 --> 01:54:09,766
...that I will always be there
for you.

1159
01:54:09,975 --> 01:54:13,937
I will always be there
to take care of you.

1160
01:54:14,938 --> 01:54:16,940
I promise you that.

1161
01:54:20,235 --> 01:54:22,529
I will always be your friend.

1162
01:54:25,449 --> 01:54:27,326
Only a friend...

1163
01:54:28,202 --> 01:54:29,745
...Peter Parker?

1164
01:54:31,914 --> 01:54:34,750
That's all I have to give.

1165
01:55:01,109 --> 01:55:03,779
Whatever life holds in store for me...

1166
01:55:03,780 --> 01:55:06,309
I will never forget these words,

1167
01:55:07,032 --> 01:55:12,079
"With great power
comes great responsibility. "

1168
01:55:12,246 --> 01:55:14,498
This is my gift.

1169
01:55:14,665 --> 01:55:16,792
My curse.

1170
01:55:17,292 --> 01:55:19,211
Who am I?

1171
01:55:19,586 --> 01:55:20,963
I'm Spiderman.

1172
01:55:21,305 --> 01:56:21,547
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
